A||||3||billfredmike24||Horn working but not well??||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||08-21-2001||11:56 PM||||My horn was not working at all so i took the white box(relay?) out from the convenience center, and put in another one from my parts car.  The horn on the right side worked on and off, and the one on the left made little beeps.  After a little while they both just made little beeps.  When i push the horn now the interior lights dim a little and in the white box you can see a green flash? and all i get is just little beeps.  <BR>If i get a new white box will this likely solve my problems? Any info. would be great.<BR>Thanks Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||08-22-2001||01:33 AM||||This may sound wierd, but check your fuse marked Batt or Battery. If it is good then check to see the speakers are grounded and clean the spade connections at the horn. Kind of a pain to get to but they can corrode.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed<BR>El Paso, TX||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-22-2001||07:22 PM||||Doesn't hurt to check the fuses<P>unplug one horn and then do the other. see what each does by itself.<P>If they still sound like hell, try putting any working horn in place of them just to check the circuit. Nearly any horn will do for a test.<P>These horns are mounted quite low. they are easy targets for road salt and stuff.<P>If they are shot then just replace them with some aftermarket ones that are nice and loud.<P>If you are going to do air horns, replace the electrics anyway and rig them both to a selector switch. Air horns can actually get you in trouble in some places. They aren't usually illegal but a pissed cop can get you for noise at night. They also piss off inspection station people.<P>Also, air horns have a nasty habit of splitting the diaphragm. it kills the whole set when that happens. having the mains in working shape give you a instant easy fix. (You'll know if/when it happens. the set will sound like an asmatic pig. been there, done that.)<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-22-2001||08:58 PM||||P.S....<P>While I was thinking about it, I remembered to go look at mine. Every so often they didn't beep.<P>One was dead the other wasn't worth much.<P>For temporary I slapped my aftermarket electrics that were sitting after being yanked off my last car.<P>I think these are Fiam ones. Much nicer sound than meep meep ones.<P>I also looked at the OE ones after I took them off.<P>You can take the actual horn off it's bracket and use it to mount the new ones. This will give you a better fit with the replacements.<P>Unless you want to redo the wire for electric horns, mount them in the OE location. Mount them mouth down and put some dielectric on the terminal to prevent corosion. ||||reg||1
